This is a very simple fix! The issue is that the fallback message hardcodes the word "Approval" or "Partial approval", even if the user clicked the Reject button.
We just need to dynamically check the modalMode (or mode) and change the word "Approval" to "Rejection" when they are rejecting the batch.
Here are the **2 exact replacements** you need to make in your **JournalAuthorization.js** file:
### 1. Fix the Main Dialog Submission (handleSubmitAction)
Find the handleSubmitAction function (around line 240).
**Find this exact block of code:**
```javascript
      const response = await callApi(
        "/JS/journals/process-bulk",
        {
          batchId: selectedBatch.batchId,
          status: modalMode,
          remarks: executorRemarks.trim(),
        },
        "POST"
      );

      const displayMessage = response?.message || "Approval process started in background. You will be notified upon completion.";
      showSnackBar(displayMessage, "info");

```
**Replace it with this:**
```javascript
      const response = await callApi(
        "/JS/journals/process-bulk",
        {
          batchId: selectedBatch.batchId,
          status: modalMode,
          remarks: executorRemarks.trim(),
        },
        "POST"
      );

      // Dynamically change text based on ACCEPTED or REJECTED
      const fallbackMsg = modalMode === "ACCEPTED" 
        ? "Approval process started in background. You will be notified upon completion."
        : "Rejection process started in background. You will be notified upon completion.";
        
      const displayMessage = response?.message || fallbackMsg;
      showSnackBar(displayMessage, "info");

```
### 2. Fix the Partial Submission (handleSubmitPartialAction)
Find the handleSubmitPartialAction function (around line 280).
**Find this exact block of code:**
```javascript
      const response = await callApi(
        "/JS/journals/process-bulk",
        {
          batchId: viewingBatchId,
          journalIdPrefixes: selectedJournalPrefixes,
          status: mode,
          remarks: partialExecutorRemarks.trim(),
        },
        "POST"
      );

      const displayMessage = response?.message || "Partial approval process started in background. You will be notified upon completion.";
      showSnackBar(displayMessage, "info");

```
**Replace it with this:**
```javascript
      const response = await callApi(
        "/JS/journals/process-bulk",
        {
          batchId: viewingBatchId,
          journalIdPrefixes: selectedJournalPrefixes,
          status: mode,
          remarks: partialExecutorRemarks.trim(),
        },
        "POST"
